S142 LRC14 AFFINE-DEPTH UNITAL CHAIN
==============================================================================
[0] Assumption challenge / quotient declaration
  considered vertices:
    runners, C27 residues, unital blocks, calibrated transfer pairs,
    affine words, suffix-depth profiles, triangular strips, K33 flags,
    and proof obligations.
  chosen quotient:
    calibrated S140 transfer components composed as affine a/b words.
  quotient preserves:
    C27 gcd depth, unital block intersections, branch order, and
    exact M/Farey labels through external metadata.
  quotient destroys:
    exact safe-time geometry and any canonical AP8 symmetry.
  challenged assumption:
    the triangular/perfect-number motif is only scalar numerology.
    Here it becomes a noncommutative depth-order certificate.

[1] Component depths from C27 strata
  depth = 1 + depth_gcd(hole) + depth_gcd(double),
  where unit,gcd3,gcd9 strata have depths 0,1,2.
  GW  GW 12->24          strata=(1, 1) depth=3 block=('AP', 'D3', 'GW', 'H12') note=AP/GW anchor block
  K33 near-miss 12->36   strata=(1, 2) depth=4 block=('D10', 'D9', 'H12', 'H9') note=near/K33 block
  P10 petal 10->20       strata=(0, 0) depth=1 block=('D7', 'D9', 'H10', 'H13') note=unit petal10 block
  P13 petal 13->26       strata=(0, 0) depth=1 block=('D1', 'D11', 'D12', 'H13') note=unit petal13 block

[2] S138 two-block splice affine strips
  ('P10', 'GW'): component_depths=[1, 3] word=babaaa suffix_depths=[4, 3] depth_sum=7 beta=3/16 union_size=8 intersections=((),)
  ('P10', 'K33'): component_depths=[1, 4] word=babaaaa suffix_depths=[5, 4] depth_sum=9 beta=3/32 union_size=7 intersections=(('D9',),)
  ('GW', 'P10'): component_depths=[3, 1] word=baaaba suffix_depths=[4, 1] depth_sum=5 beta=9/16 union_size=8 intersections=((),)
  ('K33', 'P10'): component_depths=[4, 1] word=baaaaba suffix_depths=[5, 1] depth_sum=6 beta=17/32 union_size=7 intersections=(('D9',),)
  readout:
    P10 then GW gives suffix depths [4,3] and sum 7.
    P10 then K33 gives [5,4] and sum 9, one depth level higher.
    Reversing the order changes the invariant.  The affine packet is
    noncommutative, as required by the S140 branch-local rule.

[3] S140 linked unital chain
  linked order GW -> K33 -> P10: component_depths=[3, 4, 1] word=baaabaaaaba suffix_depths=[8, 5, 1] depth_sum=14 beta=137/256 union_size=10 intersections=(('H12',), (), ('D9',))
  all permutations of the same depth multiset [3,4,1]:
