  readout:
    The S140 path order gives suffix-depth sum 14 exactly.
    The other five orders give 13,15,17,18,19.  Thus LRC14 appears
    as an order-sensitive affine-depth signature, not as a raw count.
    Triangular comparison: T_4=10, T_5=15;
    depth 14 is the interior strip between nearby triangular totals,
    selected by the AP/GW--H12--K33--D9--petal chain.

[4] Tournament Analysis
  vertices: proof carriers, not runners.
  pairwise observable:
    (M/Farey retention, unital incidence retention, affine order retention,
     finite checkability, state-lift fit, anti-scalar guard).
  switch/gauge: lexicographically larger role score wins.
    exact M/Farey branch               score=(6, 6, 6, 5, 5, 6) role=keeps p/q, q, and excess e=14p-q
    C27 unital calibrated chain        score=(5, 6, 6, 5, 5, 6) role=AP/GW--H12--near/K33--D9--petal10 packet
    affine depth-14 signature          score=(5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 6) role=noncommutative depth sum 14 for linked S140 order
    two-block splice strips            score=(5, 5, 5, 5, 4, 6) role=P10+GW and P10+K33 triangular-strip depths
    Kpq/K33 owner packet               score=(5, 4, 4, 4, 6, 5) role=p>=3 incidence and forbidden-H state-lift address
    triangular/perfect product lane    score=(4, 4, 4, 5, 3, 5) role=T_{2x-1} and p*(14p-1) product/coimage side channel
    raw scalar equality                score=(1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1) role=false equality if used without labels
  fingerprint: score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1} c3=0 hp=1
  Hamiltonian carrier order:
    exact M/Farey branch > C27 unital calibrated chain > affine depth-14 signature > two-block splice strips > Kpq/K33 owner packet > triangular/perfect product lane > raw scalar equality

[5] Proof readout
  HYP-2941 said to attach affine-depth packets after exact labels.
  HYP-2942 supplies the calibrated labels.  Under the component-depth
  rule above, the linked K33 path has affine suffix-depth sum 14.
  Candidate lemma refinement:
    In the second-gap frontier, any residual that reaches the calibrated
    AP/GW--H12--near/K33--D9--petal10 path should carry the depth-14
    affine signature.  Unit-only splices stay in lower triangular strips
    and should discharge by C27 petal/two-swap rigidity; depth-14 linked
    packets should feed the HYP-2908 / THM-572 forbidden-H state lift.
  LRC14 is not proved here.  The contribution is a concrete packet
  grammar that turns the repeated triangular/perfect-number prompt into
  an order-sensitive invariant on the known low-frontier branches.
